      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BOAB BOY (1) gets the nod off a strong Kalgoorlie third in a NMW1Y, where he sat handy, travelled well and fought on to be beaten just under a length by Sandfire Rose. He eases from provincial grade, is proven at this track and distance, and his 1600m record gives him the most rounded profile. THE CANDY KID (8) is the danger on class, having contested the Listed Boulder Cup two back before a well-held fourth over 2200m last week; back to the mile and down from that stronger company, he has the right setup to rebound. WESTERN IMPACT (5) arrives in honest form, following a Carnarvon win with second to REPEATER at Mingenew, though he has to turn that result around. REPEATER (2) beat WESTERN IMPACT by just under two lengths as favourite at Mingenew and gets weight relief with the winning rider staying on, but this is his first try around 1600m. GOT LUCKY (3) has claims off a solid performance last time out.",
